coder › Done. Implementing now complete and committed on `work/main`.

## Files changed

**`src/ini.ts`** — replaced the stub with a full implementation:
- Splits on `/\r?\n/`, tracks 1-based line numbers.
- `current = ''` initially; section objects created lazily only when a key is stored.
- Blank lines and `;`/`#` comment lines (after trim) ignored.
- Section headers: trimmed, must end with `]` and length ≥ 2, else throws `SyntaxError` containing the line number.
- Key=value: splits on first `=`, trims key (throws if empty, with line number) and unquoted value; quoted values (`"..."`) preserved verbatim including leading/trailing spaces and inner `;`. Later keys overwrite earlier in the same section.
- Any other line throws `SyntaxError` with the line number.

**`src/ini.test.ts`** — added tests covering all points (a)–(h) from the plan: keys under `''`, section assignment, whitespace trimming, `;`/`#`/blank lines, quoted values, first-= split, override, and error line numbers — plus a few extra (`[]` empty section, inline comments not stripped, `\r\n`, multiple sections, empty input).

The tests were placed in `src/ini.test.ts`, matching the existing test file and the `bun test` runner.

